# Cirak packaged unit environment (read by cirak.service).
#
# The unit already loads the token through
#   LoadCredential=token:/etc/cirak/token
# and sets CIRAK_TOKEN_FILE to the systemd credentials copy; do not repeat
# either setting here and never put a token or a password in this file.
#
# The unit creates /run/cirak-admin, /run/cirak-dashboard, /var/lib/cirak,
# /var/lib/cirak/overlay and /var/lib/cirak/writer-locks, but wires none of the
# settings below (ADR-026 section 4.4). Uncomment only what this host needs.
#
# CIRAK_ADMIN_SOCKET=/run/cirak-admin/admin.sock
# CIRAK_DASHBOARD_SOCKET=/run/cirak-dashboard/dash.sock
# CIRAK_OVERLAY_DIR=/var/lib/cirak/overlay
# CIRAK_WRITER_LOCK_DIR=/var/lib/cirak/writer-locks
# CIRAK_LIFECYCLE_CONFIG=/etc/cirak/lifecycle.json
#
# The Claude Code adapter is off by default. With ProtectHome=true and a user
# without a home, a home under the state directory is needed and that directory
# has to be added to StateDirectory= in a drop-in:
# CIRAK_CLAUDE_HOME=/var/lib/cirak/claude
